      "problem": "Sophie reserves a hotel room. The price of the room is $T$ dollars and, additionally, she must pay a $9%$ luxury tax.\n\nWhich expression gives the total cost, in dollars, of the hotel room after tax is applied?",
      "worked_solution": "The price before taxes of a hotel room is $T$ dollars.\n\nThe amount of taxes Sophie pays is  $9%$ of the price of the hotel room, or $0.09T.$\n\nTherefore, the expression that represents the total cost (in dollars) of the  hotel room after luxury tax is:\n\n \n\n$$\nT+0.09T\n$$",
